<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>A good chart marks its limits</h2>
      <p><b>The model charts evolution, not every origin question.</b> Honest navigators distinguish what the evidence-supported course describes from what remains beyond the chart.</p>
      <grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill">
        <grid-item colspan="30" background-color="surface">
          <labels><label variant="solid">Within the chart</label></labels>
          <h3>Development of the observable universe</h3>
          <p>A hot, dense early phase followed by expansion and cooling. The account includes the formation of nuclei, atoms, freely traveling light, stars, and galaxies.</p>
          <p><b>No privileged center or navigable edge is required.</b></p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="30" cell-style="outline">
          <labels><label variant="outline">Boundary marked</label></labels>
          <h3>Before the earliest described phase</h3>
          <p>What preceded that phase remains uncertain. The Big Bang model does not turn an open question into a known launch point, outer void, or certain first cause.</p>
          <p><b>The limit is part of an honest chart.</b></p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>